course: dictionary
lesson: 9621
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These words are the context, and they leave clues. «Toad struts along the high road, miles from home, singing his own praises.» The singing and the praising tell you that strutting means walking in a proud way, not holding anything up.
explain: As a verb, strut is an action word: to walk in a proud, stiff way, with your chest out and your head up. As a noun, a strut is a naming word: a bar or rod that holds up or strengthens part of something, like a bridge, a roof or an aircraft wing.
explain: Always ask which meaning fits the sentence. Swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense. If a sentence talks about bones, wings or frames, strut probably means the bar. If it talks about a character showing off, it probably means the walk.
fact: Strut is a verb: to walk in a proud, stiff way, with your chest out and your head up.
fact: Strut is also a noun: a bar or rod that holds up or strengthens part of a structure.
fact: «Strut your stuff» is informal and means to show off what you can do, especially when dancing.
fact: In design and technology, a strut pushes apart, while a tie pulls together.
fact: «Many bird bones are hollow with thin crossing struts», which keeps them light but still strong for flying.
exercise: «Toad struts along the high road, miles from home, singing his own praises.» What does strut mean here? | To fall down in a heap | *To walk in a proud way, showing off | To hold up a roof with a bar | To sleep under a tree
exercise: «Many bird bones are hollow with thin crossing struts.» In this sentence, what is a strut? | A kind of feather | A way of walking with the chest out | A happy bird song | *A bar or rod that strengthens part of the bone
exercise: Ella says, «Come on, strut your stuff at the dance!» What does strut your stuff mean? | Hide at the back of the hall | Fall over on the dance floor | *Show off what you can do, especially when dancing | Walk home early
test: In design and technology, a strut pushes apart while a tie pulls together. Which one pushes? | Wire | *Strut | Tie | Rope
test: «Guinea pigs... a deep rumble while strutting shows one is trying to be in charge.» What does strutting show here? | The guinea pig wants a bath | *The guinea pig is trying to be in charge | The guinea pig is asleep | The guinea pig is content and being stroked
exam: Which meaning fits «strut your stuff» at a talent show? | *To show off what you can do | To hide in a heap on the stage | To walk slowly home in the rain | A bar that holds up a roof
